%% SWDA Part 2A — v3 targeted precision patch/A2 | proposed local Python PoC sequence, NOT an implementation trace.
%% Only Annex A (MO-01..MO-08) and Annex B (S1..S5) may be referenced.
%% Annex A is illustrative and Annex B unverified; no simulated statement is evidence of fraud.
%% Distinct trusted controls and isolated actors; all cross-actor communication is mediated.
%%{init: {"theme": "base", "themeVariables": {"fontFamily": "Inter, Arial, sans-serif", "background": "#FFFFFF", "primaryColor": "#F4F7FB", "primaryTextColor": "#17243A", "primaryBorderColor": "#71869D", "lineColor": "#536779", "signalColor": "#40536D", "signalTextColor": "#17243A", "actorBkg": "#F4F7FB", "actorBorder": "#7890A6", "actorTextColor": "#17243A", "noteBkgColor": "#FFF7E7", "noteBorderColor": "#CBA86B", "noteTextColor": "#4F4027", "activationBkgColor": "#EAF5F1", "activationBorderColor": "#5D9883", "labelBoxBkgColor": "#EFF6FF", "labelBoxBorderColor": "#94B4D5", "labelTextColor": "#17324E"}, "sequence": {"mirrorActors": false, "showSequenceNumbers": false, "wrap": true, "useMaxWidth": false, "actorMargin": 35, "diagramMarginX": 26, "diagramMarginY": 24, "messageMargin": 27, "noteMargin": 12, "boxMargin": 10, "boxTextMargin": 6}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor H as Human operator / reviewer
    box rgb(237,245,252) Trusted local control and provenance
        participant CLI as Local CLI / review UI
        participant ORCH as Deterministic orchestrator
        participant CAT as Read-only source catalogue
        participant POL as Policy / schema gateway
    end
    box rgb(246,242,255) Isolated scripted actors
        participant TA as Trainee Agent
        participant PA as Training Provider Agent
        participant EA as Employer Agent
    end
    box rgb(239,246,251) Trusted deterministic analysis
        participant ANA as Pattern assembler / actor-removal
    end
    box rgb(255,246,230) ISOLATED NON-AUTHORITATIVE REVIEW
        participant REV as Review Agent - recommendations only
    end
    box rgb(237,249,244) Trusted deterministic assurance
        participant SAFE as Deterministic safety gates
        participant EVAL as Evaluation harness
    end
    box rgb(232,247,238) Trusted human decision and persistence
        participant APPR as Trusted human approval service
        participant STORE as Trusted run state + audit store
    end

    Note over H,CAT: PHASE 1 — INITIATION AND SOURCE TRUST BOUNDARY
    H->>CLI: Start simulation with selected scenario
    CLI->>ORCH: Authorised invocation + versioned config
    ORCH->>STORE: Create CANDIDATE run_id, seed, NON_APPROVED state and aggregate lineage budget
    ORCH->>CAT: Resolve Annex A MO-01..MO-08 and Annex B S1..S5 IDs
    CAT->>CAT: Compare ID, schema, version and digest with separately trusted versioned manifest
    Note over CAT,POL: Source text is untrusted DATA, never executable policy or instructions.
    alt Source references and scenario are valid
        CAT-->>ORCH: Pinned catalogue snapshot + provenance / trust tags
        ORCH->>POL: Install fixed actor scopes, sender / recipient ACL and schemas
        POL-->>ORCH: Policy snapshot validated
        ORCH->>STORE: Checkpoint caps: patterns, CF, TEST fixtures, turns, retries, elapsed and aggregate lineage calls
    else Missing / malformed / altered source or invalid permissions
        CAT-->>ORCH: Validation failure + quarantine reason
        ORCH->>STORE: Append failed initiation event, state BLOCKED
        break Invalid initiation, terminate run
            ORCH-->>CLI: Terminal failure, no agent execution
        end
    end

    Note over ORCH,EA: PHASE 2 — BOUNDED, GATEWAY-MEDIATED SIMULATION (valid runs only)
    loop Each scheduled actor turn, within round / step / time / aggregate lineage call budgets
        ORCH->>CAT: Read only source IDs permitted to selected actor
        CAT-->>ORCH: Scoped, tagged excerpts, no privileged records
        ORCH->>POL: Dispatch envelope (run_id, msg_id, sender, target, scope, schema)
        alt Dispatch authorised and within budget
            POL->>STORE: Append dispatch ALLOW + source versions / msg_id
            alt Selected turn: Trainee Agent
                POL->>TA: Scoped context + optional validated prior message
                TA->>TA: Invoke scripted trainee mock LLM
                TA-->>POL: Proposed structured message (not a fact)
            else Selected turn: Training Provider Agent
                POL->>PA: Scoped context + optional validated prior message
                PA->>PA: Invoke scripted provider mock LLM
                PA-->>POL: Proposed structured message (not a fact)
            else Selected turn: Employer Agent
                POL->>EA: Scoped context + optional validated prior message
                EA->>EA: Invoke scripted employer mock LLM
                EA-->>POL: Proposed structured message (not a fact)
            end
            POL->>POL: Verify bound sender / recipient / ACL / source IDs / schema / safety
            alt Valid actor response and permitted recipient
                POL->>STORE: Append receipt ALLOW (run_id, msg_id, policy outcome)
                POL-->>ORCH: Validated message + provenance / intended recipient
                opt A different actor must receive this message
                    ORCH->>POL: Schedule recipient turn with validated parent msg_id
                    Note over ORCH,POL: No actor-to-actor channel, next delivery repeats dispatch checks.
                end
            else Retryable schema error and retry budget remains
                POL->>STORE: Append receipt DENY + validation reason
                POL-->>ORCH: Retryable error + attempt number
                ORCH->>STORE: Increment retry / usage counters
                ORCH->>ORCH: Requeue same scoped task only; no additional sources, recipients or permissions
            else Non-retryable policy / safety failure or retry exhausted
                POL->>STORE: Append receipt DENY + reason + msg_id
                POL-->>ORCH: Block message, never deliver it
                ORCH->>STORE: Record terminal fault or continue by configured policy
            end
        else Dispatch denied or resource limit reached
            POL->>STORE: Append dispatch DENY / limit event
            POL-->>ORCH: Reject request + reason code
            ORCH->>STORE: Stop / mark incomplete on configured fail-closed rule
        end
        ORCH->>STORE: Checkpoint round, route, retries, mock usage and remaining budget
    end
    ORCH->>STORE: Seal run transcript, status COMPLETED or BLOCKED
    Note over ORCH,STORE: Blocked or incomplete runs do not enter candidate approval, all actor activity is recorded by trusted code.

    alt Completed with sufficient validated contributions
        Note over ORCH,ANA: PHASE 3 — HYPOTHETICAL PATTERN CONSTRUCTION
        ORCH->>ANA: Validated transcript + allowed source / simulation provenance
        ANA->>ANA: Typed risk-level card: actors, contributions, benefits, flows, test-data needs; bounded pattern count
        ANA->>ANA: Label each assertion SOURCE / SIMULATION / ASSUMPTION
        loop Each actor actually participating, up to configured CF cap (CANDIDATE only)
            ANA->>ORCH: Request CF: CANDIDATE parent_run_id + removed_actor, seed / ACL / lineage budget
            ORCH->>ORCH: Enforce parent=CANDIDATE, depth=1, cap; fresh CF ID and context, remove tainted descendants
            ORCH->>CAT: Reload immutable Annex-only baseline for remaining actor scopes
            CAT-->>ORCH: Fresh scoped source snapshot + versioned provenance
            ORCH->>POL: CF bounded rerun: remaining actors, SAME policy / schemas, aggregate lineage budget
            Note over ORCH,POL: CF never launches CF/TEST; no removed-actor memory or descendant data; failures fail closed.
            POL-->>ORCH: Validated reduced-actor outcome / fault
            ORCH->>STORE: Append linked counterfactual run and messages
            ORCH-->>ANA: Independent reduced outcome + trace reference
        end
        ANA->>ANA: Separate multi-party collusion / single-actor / inconclusive
        ANA->>STORE: Append draft card ID, provenance and dependency outcomes

        Note over ANA,SAFE: PHASE 4 — INDEPENDENT MACHINE REVIEW AND DETERMINISTIC GATES
        ANA->>REV: Draft hypothetical card + dependency results + source IDs
        REV->>POL: Request scoped source/MO lookup (reviewer identity, purpose, allowed IDs only)
        alt Reviewer read authorised — references valid
            POL->>CAT: Invoke trusted read-only MO/reference helpers for allowed MO/S source IDs
            CAT-->>POL: Versioned, tagged permitted records via read-only helper; no unrestricted catalogue
            POL-->>REV: Schema-validated, filtered references, trust labels and comparison inputs
            REV->>REV: Challenge assumptions, evidence strength, benign conflicts and data gaps
            REV-->>SAFE: Recommend known / variation / new relative to sample only
        else Reviewer ACL denied, invalid source or unapproved tool
            POL->>STORE: Append review DENY, source ID and reason
            POL-->>REV: Deny — no catalogue data or private actor state
            REV-->>SAFE: Review invalid — mandatory deterministic gate failure
        end
        Note over REV,SAFE: REV is less trusted than SAFE/EVAL/APPR; never writes catalogue, gates, audit or approval.
        SAFE->>SAFE: Schema, provenance, injection, unsafe-detail and source/simulation checks
        SAFE->>EVAL: Evaluate candidate run and policy / actor / E2E assertions
        EVAL->>STORE: Read run-linked messages, denials, budgets and prior gate outcomes
        STORE-->>EVAL: Read-only trace / audit evidence
        EVAL-->>SAFE: Evaluation report with failures and run_id
        alt Safety / provenance / evaluation gates fail
            SAFE->>STORE: Append blocked candidate + specific failure reasons
            SAFE-->>ORCH: BLOCKED, no human approval queue entry
            ORCH-->>CLI: Report failed candidate for diagnostics only
        else All gates pass
            SAFE->>STORE: Candidate-only: persist passed gates and REVIEW_PENDING; CF/TEST cannot queue
            SAFE-->>ORCH: Reviewable candidate (never a fraud finding)

            Note over H,SAFE: PHASE 5 — EXPLICIT HUMAN-ONLY DECISION
            ORCH->>CLI: Display tagged card, assumptions, source IDs, MO basis, tests
            CLI-->>H: Present simulated risk pattern for investigation decision
            H->>CLI: Submit explicit decision with reason
            CLI->>APPR: Submit human-origin decision + reviewer identity / reason
            APPR->>POL: Verify configured/local PoC reviewer identity, role and action scope
            POL-->>APPR: Explicit reviewer-authorisation verdict
            APPR->>STORE: Read candidate status REVIEW_PENDING + persisted gate IDs
            STORE-->>APPR: Current status / validation / evaluation evidence
            alt Authorised human, REVIEW_PENDING, passed gates and valid action
                alt Approve for further investigation
                    APPR->>STORE: Atomic compare-and-swap: APPROVED_FOR_INVESTIGATION + decision audit
                else Reject candidate
                    APPR->>STORE: Atomic compare-and-swap: REJECTED + decision audit
                else Request revision
                    APPR->>STORE: Atomic compare-and-swap: REVISION_REQUESTED + decision audit
                end
                Note over APPR,STORE: One SQLite CAS transaction verifies REVIEW_PENDING + gates and persists decision; no enterprise IAM asserted.
                STORE-->>APPR: Committed decision receipt (or conflict/failure)
                APPR-->>CLI: Return committed receipt — on failure return denial only
                CLI-->>H: Persisted decision receipt — no fraud finding
            else Model-originated, unauthorised, malformed or invalid state / gates
                APPR->>STORE: Append denied attempt without candidate-state change
                APPR-->>CLI: Deny — status unchanged (no automatic approval)
                CLI-->>H: Denied decision, no state transition
            end
        end
    else Blocked / incomplete / no valid candidate
        ORCH-->>CLI: Terminal outcome, no reviewable card or approval transition
    end

    Note over ORCH,STORE: PHASE 6 — REPLAYABLE EVALUATION AND OBSERVABILITY (separate test-only runs)
    opt On-demand or pre-submission deterministic regression suite
        EVAL->>ORCH: Start independent top-level TEST fixtures within suite cap; not from TEST or CF
        ORCH->>POL: TEST via SAME gateway/schema, bounded turns/retries/usage; no recursive TEST
        POL-->>ORCH: Fixture responses / denial codes (through bounded turns)
        ORCH->>STORE: Append test-only run IDs, message IDs, seeds and budgets
        EVAL->>STORE: Inspect fixture outputs, policy decisions and complete traces
        STORE-->>EVAL: Trace snapshots correlated to fixture run IDs
        EVAL->>EVAL: Check expected denials, benign outcomes, schema / E2E regressions
        EVAL->>STORE: Append test report only; no human queue, no cascading TEST or approval writes
    end
    Note over H,STORE: AUDIT: actors, REV, CF, TEST and EVAL never write approval states — only APPR persists human decisions.
